{"absent":["Register address offset and software access path for the second event register are not shown in these fragments.","Clearing acknowledgment and interrupt delivery semantics beyond readable and writable marking are not shown.","Functional meaning of accelerator interval dashboard and clock indicators is not shown.","Complete generation two bitfield tail and generation five shift mask defines are outside the routed range.","Locking concurrency and caller context rules for this register are not shown.","Entry points exports and state transitions using these definitions are not shown."],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_MESSAGE_ACCELERATOR_INT0_SHFT"],"text":"UV4 second event register assigns one bit per message accelerator interrupt in low order with numeric position equal to interrupt number. The routed portion confirms numbers five through fifteen at positions five through fifteen each with a single bit mask and continues the zero based scheme named by the header."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_MESSAGE_ACCELERATOR_INT0_SHFT"],"text":"UV4 second event register places a clock interval indicator at position sixteen and a dashboard indicator at position seventeen then thirty two clock indicators at positions eighteen through forty nine in numeric order. Every member is one bit wide with a one hot mask so the clock group spans eighteen to forty nine inclusive."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_0_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_0_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_1_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_1_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_2_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_2_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv