CCURRED2_RTC_25_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_26_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_26_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_27_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_27_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_28_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_28_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_29_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_29_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_30_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_30_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_31_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_31_MASK"],"text":"UV2 second event register packs thirty two clock indicators into the low thirty two bits one bit each in numeric order. Indicator zero uses position zero with low bit alone set and indicator thirty one uses position thirty one with that bit alone set and each intermediate indicator uses its own index as position with only that bit set."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_1_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_1_SHFT"],"text":"Version independent access for clock indicator one selects position and mask by probed hardware generation. The mask is eight for generation five and bit nineteen alone for generation four and bit one alone for generations three and two with zero when generation is unknown. The position is three for generation five and nineteen for generation four and one for generations three and two with negative one as invalid sentinel otherwise."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u"],"text":"Second event status is a sixty four bit scalar that can also be viewed through generation specific field layouts. The scalar view holds the raw register value while each structured view splits the same sixty four bits into named one bit indicators plus a reserved high portion with member order from least significant upward."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u.uvyh_event_occurred2_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u.uv5h_event_occurred2_s"],"text":"Common and generation five views share the same arrangement. Two leading one bit control indicators for interval and dashboard come first followed in numeric order by thirty two one bit clock indicators then thirty high bits marked reserved. All indicator members permit read and write access."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u.uv4h_event_occurred2_s"],"text":"Generation four view widens the low portion. Sixteen one bit accelerator indicators come first in numeric order then the interval and dashboard control indicators then thirty two one bit clock indicators in numeric order leaving fourteen high bits reserved. All named members permit read and write access."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u.uv3h_event_occurred2_s"],"text":"Generation three view places thirty two one bit clock indicators in numeric order starting at the least significant bit with the upper thirty two bits reserved. All clock members permit read and write access."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u.uv2h_event_occurred2_s"],"text":"Generation two view begins with the same low order clock indicators as generation three and shows at least the first few indicators each as a one bit read write member starting from indicator zero. The routed range truncates after the early members so the remainder is not visible here though sibling defines imply a matching thirty two bit low group."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u.uvyh_event_occurred2_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u.uv4h_event_occurred2_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u.uv3h_event_occurred2_s"],"text":"All second event indicator fields are one bit wide with disjoint one hot masks and each structured view totals sixty four bits including its reserved high field. Reserved size varies by generation to pad the defined low bits up to sixty four and every defined indicator is marked readable and writable."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_1_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_1_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvyh_event_occurred2_u"],"text":"Bit positions for the same logical indicator move across hardware generations so interpreting the register with the wrong generation view misattributes interrupts. Clock indicator one lives at different positions on newer versus older hardware. Callers must branch on probed generation before applying masks or shifts and must treat the unknown generation sentinel as invalid rather than shifting by it."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":77,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"90fbc6904033e42000ae762f7e22713ee62f438dcdedfc4bd7328bc76c81714c","prompt_sha256":"b0d48ef155173c6011053e635f4423fa2e960f190d83a1be4facb72bd8e00c02","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_MESSAGE_ACCELERATOR_INT0_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_0_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV2H_EVENT_OCCURRED2_RTC_0_SHFT"]}
